<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103097" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέραμνον</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέρεμνον</span></b> , τό, a word used esp. by <i><span class="en">
			E.
		</span></i>, but only in pl. and always (except once, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέραμνά τ᾽ οἴκων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Hipp.</u>
					418
				</span></i>
			) in lyr. passages, <i>chamber, house</i>, 
				like
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέλαθρα, τ. ἀπὸ
				νυμφιδίων</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				768
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παστάδων ὑπὲρ τ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Or.</u>
				1371
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Περγάμων . . καταίθεται
			τ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Tr.</u>
				1296
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ Ἀΐδα τεράμνων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Alc.</u>
					457
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ Πυθίοις τ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				536
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὲρ τέραμνα</span>
			<u>Ph.</u>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				333
			</span></i>: dat. sg. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεράμνῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Maiist.
					12
				</span></i>
			: also in late Prose, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέρεμνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Artem.
					2.10
				</span></i>
			. [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-εμνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Or.</u>
					1371
				</span></i>
			 codd. ALP, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ph.</u>
				333
			</span></i> codd. VA, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				418
			</span></i> codd. exc. L, which has <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-α-</span>: <i><span class="en">
				Maiist.
			</span></i> l.c. corroborates the spelling <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-αμνον</span>.]</div>
